{
 "status": "draft",
 "_provenance": "People, places and organisations named in the Albani Zaria sermons. Candidates came from a named-entity model run once, offline, over the transcripts (MasakhaNER: masakhane/afroxlmr-large-ner-masakhaner-1.0_2.0, November 2026; hand-checked precision about 95% for people, 90% for places, 50% for organisations); the list below was then curated by hand and the model plays no further part. The generator counts only the aliases listed here, matched on the folded surface form (not the merged match key, which would read 'maka', for you, as Makka). An alias is kept only when its sense is settled in this corpus: bare 'isa' (also a verb), 'shehu' (any shaykh), 'albani' (the preacher or his Syrian namesake), 'nuhu', 'daura' (to tie) and 'kathir' (many) are left out, so counts are floors, not totals. Coordinates come from the IWAC index where it has the place (`iwac`), otherwise from Wikidata (`wikidata`, P625). Awaiting review by a Hausa-speaking specialist.",
